            <ArticleTitle>Axoplasmic transport block reduces ectopic impulse generation in injured peripheral nerves.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>73-85</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Afferent fibers ending in nerve end neuromas in rats generate a substantial ectopic discharge and are sensitive to light pressure and to circulating adrenaline. Treatment of the nerve with colchicine or vinblastine at the time of the nerve section resulted in a dose-dependent reduction in the extent of this discharge. Such treatment also reduced neuroma discharge that had already gotten underway.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
